"About intro" = "FlowTrace is a menu-bar network monitor: live per-process download/upload rates, today and period totals, quota alerts, unusual-traffic alerts, a network heatmap and per-process history analysis.";
"About statistics" = "How stats work: menu-bar and popover rates and the today and period totals are sampled every second and summed live — the period follows the Quota setting (day / week / month); the history window (process stats, network heatmap, alert log) is persisted per minute and lags by about a minute.";
"About privacy" = "Privacy: all data stays on this Mac in a local SQLite database. The app itself makes no network requests and uploads nothing.";
"About tech note" = "Technical notes: traffic figures come from the system nettop interface (kernel counters, same source as Activity Monitor); local SQLite storage, zero third-party dependencies; the interface ships in Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, English, Japanese, Spanish and more (switchable in General); appearance follows system, light or dark.";
